D('P0171','System too lean (Bank 1)',SYS.fuel,2,'The engine is getting too much air or too little fuel, and the computer has run out of room to correct it. Long-term fuel trim is usually above +20 %.',['Vacuum leak (cracked hose, intake gasket, PCV valve)','Dirty or faulty MAF sensor','Weak fuel pump or clogged fuel filter','Clogged or leaking injectors','Exhaust leak before the upstream O2 sensor'],['Read fuel trims at idle and at 2500 rpm: if trims fall at higher rpm, suspect a vacuum leak; if they rise, suspect fuel delivery','Smoke-test the intake for vacuum leaks','Clean the MAF sensor','Measure fuel pressure','Check PCV valve and hoses']);
